Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageCompletion.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp filename
catalog generation and SciEdit.cpp completion matching under GPL version 2 or
later, retaining their TortoiseGit/TortoiseSVN copyright notices. The native
popup reuses the upstream file.ico unchanged; its provenance is recorded in
Sources/TurtleGitCore/Resources/Icons/provenance.json.

Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageSnippets.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp snippet parsing
and selection expansion, under GPL version 2 or later with its TortoiseGit
copyright notice. The original shipped snippet.txt and snippet.ico are retained
unchanged, with pinned source and SHA-256 provenance in their resource folders.

The helper also adapts CommitDlg.cpp::ScanFile capture-group extraction under
GPL version 2 or later. MessageCodeSymbols.swift adapts its definition parsing
and capture transport, retaining TortoiseGit attribution. The original
autolist.txt is bundled unchanged with pinned provenance. File scanning and
complete native code-completion integration remain under development.

MessageCodeText.swift adapts TortoiseGitMerge FileTextLines.cpp encoding detection
and decode-filter units, under GPL version 2 or later. Copyright (C) 2016, 2019,
2021, 2023, 2025 TortoiseGit and (C) 2007-2016, 2019 TortoiseSVN. Windows ACP and
malformed UTF-8 decoding require documented native adaptations.

MessageCodeScanner.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp changed-file traversal, catalog
insertion order, regex caching, timeout and size gates under GPL version 2 or
later, retaining its TortoiseGit notice. Raw decoded UTF-16 units are passed
unchanged through the existing helper transport. The native Commit popup consumes this catalog with the original code.ico
artwork. Complete editor parity and signed sandbox acceptance remain under
development.

